I'd make the actual LeaseOS road graph richer than OSM

This becomes our canonical object:

RoadEdge {
    edge_id

    // geometry
    geometry
    start_node
    end_node

    // OSM
    osm_id
    road_name
    road_ref
    road_class

    // physical
    surface
    grade
    width
    clearance
    bridge
    tunnel

    // legal
    max_weight
    max_axle
    max_height
    max_width
    max_length
    hgv_access
    dangerous_goods

    // back road
    resource_road
    lease_road
    forestry_road
    private_road
    range_road
    township_road

    // communications
    radio_required
    radio_channel
    calling_direction

    // authority
    province
    municipality
    county_md
    road_authority

    // dynamic
    current_condition
    closure_state
    live_restriction

    // provenance
    sources[]
    source_updated_at
}

That gives us a major advantage:

OSM doesn't have to contain everything.

One road can be enriched by several independent sources:

OSM
   └── geometry

511
   └── live closure

Alberta government
   └── bridge restriction

County
   └── 75% road ban

LeaseOS company data
   └── preferred haul road

Driver verified data
   └── radio channel

Client
   └── lease gate / access notes

All of those attach to the same road edge.


